{
  "id": "waterloo",
  "title": "Waterloo",
  "date": "18 June 1815",
  "blurb": "The decisive battle. Wellington's army lies behind the crest of Mont-Saint-Jean, out of sight of the French guns, with the walled farms of Hougoumont, La Haye Sainte and Papelotte flung forward like breakwaters. Napoleon must break it before Blücher's Prussians come through the Bois de Paris onto his right flank. The ground is soaked; the Emperor waits for it to dry. Every regiment still in your roster fights here.",
  "hint": "The ridge hides Wellington's reserves until you crest it. Hougoumont sits behind its wood out on the left; La Haye Sainte guards the Brussels road. The Prussians come out of the woods to the east around mid-afternoon and drive on Plancenoit: hold it or lose your line of retreat. Keep the Guard for the last throw.",
